1. Definitions

1.1 "AnchorShell" or "Licensor" means AnchorShell Inc.

1.2 "Software" means the AnchorShell Relay Community Edition source code,
object code, documentation, and other materials distributed with this license,
including modifications and derivative works based on them.

1.3 "You" or "Licensee" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights
under this license.

1.4 "Affiliate" means any entity that directly or indirectly controls, is
controlled by, or is under common control with You. "Control" means ownership
of more than fifty percent (50%) of the voting interests of an entity, or the
power to direct its management.

1.5 "Aggregate Gross Revenue" means the total gross revenue of You and all of
Your Affiliates during the immediately preceding twelve (12) months, before
expenses, excluding taxes collected for a government and excluding
intercompany transfers counted elsewhere in the same consolidated group.

1.6 "Small Business" means a Licensee whose Aggregate Gross Revenue is less
than US$1,000,000 (or the equivalent amount in another currency).

1.7 "Personal or Noncommercial Use" means use by an individual for personal,
educational, evaluation, research, hobby, or other noncommercial purposes that
is not performed for or on behalf of a business or other revenue-generating
organization.

1.8 "Commercial Use" means any use, copying, modification, distribution,
hosting, deployment, or integration of the Software by or for a business,
organization, or other activity connected with commercial operations,
revenue-generating activity, or internal business operations.

1.9 "Reserved Commercial Features" means the functionality listed in Schedule A,
including substantially equivalent functionality regardless of its name, user
interface, protocol, or implementation.

1.10 "Managed Relay Service" means a product or service whose primary purpose is
to provide third parties with hosted, managed, or remote access to the Software,
or to substantially equivalent Relay gateway functionality derived from the
Software. A separate product that merely uses Relay internally as one component
of a materially different product or service is not a Managed Relay Service.

1.11 "Competing Relay Product" means a modified or derivative version of the
Software whose primary purpose is to provide a practical substitute for a paid
AnchorShell Relay product or service.

