Schedule A — Reserved Commercial Features

The following are Reserved Commercial Features for purposes of this license.
The restriction applies to substantially equivalent functionality, regardless
of its name or presentation.

A. Smart Groups and Smart Routing
   Request-characterization-, intent-, policy-, or classification-driven
   automatic selection among models, including configurable assignments,
   confidence-based selection, or equivalent intelligent model-selection
   behavior beyond ordinary manually configured groups and fallback ordering.

B. Multi-User Teams and Organizations
   Multiple separately authenticated human users within a shared Relay
   deployment, including invitations, organization membership, team membership,
   or shared organization administration.

C. Granular Permissions and Role-Based Access Control
   User-, role-, team-, or identity-scoped permissions controlling access to
   Relay administration, providers, routing, settings, usage, logs, queues,
   limits, or related functionality.

D. Managed API Keys
   Multiple individually attributable, revocable, scoped, or user/workload-
   specific Relay API keys beyond the single deployment-level credentials
   provided by the Community Edition.

E. Per-User and Per-Key Budgets or Limits
   Request, token, spending, provider, model, or other usage limits applied to
   individual users, managed API keys, workloads, or equivalent identities.

F. User and API-Key Usage Attribution
   Attribution, filtering, accounting, or visibility of requests, tokens,
   costs, limits, logs, or usage by individual user, managed API key, workload,
   or equivalent identity.

G. Connected Subscription Accounts
   Provider-account authorization flows, subscription-account connections,
   account pairing, managed credential lifecycle, provider quota
   synchronization, model discovery tied to subscription accounts, or access
   grants for connected provider accounts.

H. Classification Feedback and Review
   Product functionality for reviewing, correcting, labeling, or managing
   Relay request-classification results or feedback at an organizational or
   multi-user level.

I. Enterprise Identity Management
   SSO, SAML, organization-wide OIDC identity integration, SCIM provisioning,
   enterprise directory synchronization, or substantially equivalent
   enterprise identity-management functionality.

